## 3. Layout primitives (Dashboard)

| Context | Pattern |
|---|---|
| Page container | `<div className="space-y-4 p-6 lg:p-8">` |
| Page title | Always `PageHeader` (`title` + optional `subtitle` + optional `back`). Actions = `children` (not an `action` prop). |
| Content sections (data, lists, metrics) | `SectionCard` (flat, thin border, no shadow) |
| Settings / account pages (section switcher) | Parent: `flex flex-col gap-4 md:flex-row md:gap-8`. Nav via shared `NavList` (`components/dashboard/nav-list.tsx`): **`< md`** = full-width `Select` ; **`md+`** = left rail (`w-48`). Content: `min-w-0 flex-1` (+ `SectionCard` when needed). Same pattern for Account, Offers/Products editors, Forms hub/editor, Campaigns editor. |
| Metric strips | Flat label + value inside one `SectionCard` (`grid gap-6 …`). No `StatCard`, no nested metric cards. Mirror Overview. |

### Nested surfaces (avoid white-on-white)

When stacking bordered blocks inside a panel, dialog, or builder (CRM side panel sections, segment condition rows, etc.):

- Outer shell: `border border-border` on `bg-background` / `bg-card` (or no fill)
- Inner rows / nested groups: `rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-2|p-3`
- Do **not** nest multiple `bg-background` / `bg-card` boxes. That reads as “stack on stack”
- Controls inside muted rows stay on their default control surface (outline / input tokens)

Reference: CRM lead side panel blocks ; Campaigns segment condition rows.

